Honestly, most of these would wash over me. Scary pictures and warnings I've seen a hundred times on fags and booze, and they just make me think "yeah, yeah." Calorie numbers are more useful, but I'm not counting calories when I'm skint and knackered after a shift. What actually sways me is price: a reduced sticker or a cheap pack. Labels don't change that much. The fruit pot next to the Dairy Milk doesn't help if it costs more, and I'm not going to be the one reading tiny print at the till.

The text-only warnings feel a bit like being told off, and the calorie badges at least give me a number I can compare. So I'd give most of the points to the calorie-only option, a bit to the one with both, and nothing much to the rest.

