Honestly, most of these would wash over me. The graphic photos on A and E would just make me wince and look away, and a bowel tumour on a Doritos packet doesn't change what I'm going to grab at the vending machine when I've got £1.40 in my pocket. The text-only warnings in C and F are the same story: I've seen "eat less, move more" on everything for years.

A calorie count is the only thing here that gives me something to actually use. I don't count calories, but if I can see 95 next to the fruit pot and 240 next to the Dairy Milk, I'd probably think twice, especially after the trousers business. Still, I'd be weighing that against price, so it wouldn't flip much on its own. B is just the vending machine as normal, so nothing changes there.

