Honestly, the scary pictures would just make me roll my eyes. I've seen enough of that kind of thing and I'm not going to change what I buy because someone's showing me a bowel. The plain text warnings are the same, I'd read the first line and move on. A bold calorie number is the only bit I'd actually glance at, and even then I'd probably only use it if I were choosing between two things that looked similar. I'm not counting anything, so a number on its own doesn't do much. Still, it's the one thing that gives me something to compare.

Mostly I'd carry on as normal: yoghurt off the reduced shelf, a biscuit with my tea.

